01:02:31.900 --> 01:02:34.580
It's normally hotter inside
your house, 35 degrees.

01:02:34.580 --> 01:02:36.583
It's hell, I hate it so much.

01:02:36.583 --> 01:02:38.510
I was like in tears every day.

01:02:38.510 --> 01:02:41.780
Like, "I just can't do it.
I can't be here anymore."

01:02:43.210 --> 01:02:45.130
- How is the weather in Thailand?

01:02:45.130 --> 01:02:46.690
- It's similar to what we have now.

01:02:46.690 --> 01:02:48.713
So it's very hot, very humid.

01:02:49.630 --> 01:02:51.447
- For all year round?
- All year round.

01:02:51.447 --> 01:02:53.560
But our homes are designed for it.

01:02:53.560 --> 01:02:56.260
We have very thin walls and everything.

01:02:56.260 --> 01:02:58.840
So it's designed to get as
much heat out as possible.

01:02:58.840 --> 01:03:01.670
And there's AC everywhere you go as well.

01:03:01.670 --> 01:03:04.741
- It's unfair, you max
the Thai skill tree.

01:03:04.741 --> 01:03:06.083
I went down just the
British, I don't even know

01:03:06.083 --> 01:03:07.750
what you get in the British skill tree,

01:03:07.750 --> 01:03:09.906
just poor taste in food.

01:03:09.906 --> 01:03:10.840
(laughter)

01:03:10.840 --> 01:03:11.673
Unfair.

01:03:11.673 --> 01:03:12.910
- This is just out of nowhere question

01:03:12.910 --> 01:03:16.660
but how is milk in each country.

01:03:16.660 --> 01:03:19.690
I've been told by my
friend in California that,

01:03:19.690 --> 01:03:21.070
we were just talking about Baskin-Robbins

01:03:21.070 --> 01:03:24.160
because we have always,
each year they have Pokemon

01:03:24.160 --> 01:03:26.103
collaboration at Baskin-Robbins.

01:03:28.010 --> 01:03:30.520
He was complaining that milk here

01:03:30.520 --> 01:03:32.080
or ice cream here is too heavy

01:03:32.080 --> 01:03:35.827
because of the milk,
because we use whole milk.

01:03:35.827 --> 01:03:39.057
In California, they prefer low fat or-

01:03:39.057 --> 01:03:40.294
- Grass-fed milk.

01:03:40.294 --> 01:03:43.260
(laughter)

01:03:43.260 --> 01:03:44.093
- Organic.

01:03:44.093 --> 01:03:46.330
- Organic grass-fed milk.

01:03:46.330 --> 01:03:48.003
- I didn't notice that

01:03:48.003 --> 01:03:50.660
because I realized now when
you told me that the other day,

01:03:50.660 --> 01:03:53.597
I was like, "Wait, there's
never any semi skimmed

01:03:53.597 --> 01:03:55.413
"or no fat milk option here."

01:03:55.413 --> 01:03:58.525
You can order at Starbucks, but-

01:03:58.525 --> 01:04:01.000
- You can buy low-fat
milk at supermarkets.

01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.610
- Can you? I never see it.

01:04:02.610 --> 01:04:05.040
- The supermarket near
my house has skim milk,

01:04:05.040 --> 01:04:08.520
low fat milk, high calcium
milk, stuff like that.

01:04:08.520 --> 01:04:09.353
- I always wondered, I was like,

01:04:09.353 --> 01:04:13.080
"Why does milk tastes so
rich when I came here?"

01:04:13.080 --> 01:04:13.913
I'm like, "This is weird."

01:04:13.913 --> 01:04:16.158
- It's that 100% cream stuff.

01:04:16.158 --> 01:04:18.727
- I always get the half
back 'cause I'm like-

01:04:18.727 --> 01:04:21.685
- I like the thick stuff
because in Australia-

01:04:21.685 --> 01:04:23.935
(laughter)

01:04:25.030 --> 01:04:27.270
- He likes the thick stuff, Luke.

01:04:27.270 --> 01:04:29.187
- I like my dummy thicc milk.

01:04:29.187 --> 01:04:30.250
I like my dummy thicc milk

01:04:30.250 --> 01:04:32.330
because in Australia as well

01:04:32.330 --> 01:04:34.350
we didn't really have a
whole, it's like Japan,

01:04:34.350 --> 01:04:36.720
we don't really have a
whole variety of milk.

01:04:36.720 --> 01:04:38.210
Obviously, we have the full cream stuff

01:04:38.210 --> 01:04:39.940
and the low fat stuff

01:04:39.940 --> 01:04:41.717
but it's not like America where it's like

01:04:41.717 --> 01:04:45.090
"Would you like 1%, 2%, 5%, 10%?"

01:04:45.090 --> 01:04:49.520
It's like, "Just give me
milk. I just want milk."

01:04:49.520 --> 01:04:51.640
- I haven't noticed much
of a difference 'cause

01:04:51.640 --> 01:04:53.390
I don't normally, I don't know.

01:04:53.390 --> 01:04:55.800
I only have milk with my coffee.

01:04:55.800 --> 01:04:58.410
And I don't eat ice
cream too often either.

01:04:58.410 --> 01:04:59.870
- I'm not a fan of soft serve.

01:04:59.870 --> 01:05:01.550
And that seems to be
the most popular thing.

01:05:01.550 --> 01:05:02.840
- I really like soft serve.

01:05:02.840 --> 01:05:04.300
- It's too milky.

01:05:04.300 --> 01:05:06.430
If I want milk, I'll just drink milk.

01:05:06.430 --> 01:05:08.723
I want ice cream not ice
cream that tastes like milk.

01:05:08.723 --> 01:05:11.700
- Well, then just don't get
the vanilla flavor stuff,

01:05:11.700 --> 01:05:14.120
get the weirder soft serve.

01:05:14.120 --> 01:05:16.602
- True. Like matcha soft
serve is pretty good,

01:05:16.602 --> 01:05:17.435
but just no more vanilla.

01:05:17.435 --> 01:05:19.409
- Matcha, black sesame is really good.

01:05:19.409 --> 01:05:21.410
- But vanilla is my favorite
flavor of ice cream.

01:05:21.410 --> 01:05:22.520
- Well, then stop complaining,

01:05:22.520 --> 01:05:23.550
(laughter)

01:05:23.550 --> 01:05:25.060
Just eat your damn soft serve.

01:05:25.060 --> 01:05:26.170
- In Japan as well,

01:05:26.170 --> 01:05:28.690
for some reason, Baskin-Robbins
is referred to as 31.

01:05:28.690 --> 01:05:30.299
Why, what's up with that?

01:05:30.299 --> 01:05:31.340
Who made this?

01:05:31.340 --> 01:05:33.680
- It's because Baskin-Robbins,
I think might be

01:05:33.680 --> 01:05:35.536
too difficult to pronounce.
- Yeah, too long.

01:05:35.536 --> 01:05:38.270
- 'Cause I remember I
showed my Japanese cousin,

01:05:38.270 --> 01:05:39.878
'cause she loves 31 ice cream,

01:05:39.878 --> 01:05:41.423
(in foreign language) as they call it.

01:05:42.340 --> 01:05:44.987
And when I heard her
first say that, I was like

01:05:44.987 --> 01:05:45.827
"31, what's that?

01:05:45.827 --> 01:05:48.007
"That must be a Japanese
brand or something

01:05:48.007 --> 01:05:48.840
"that I don't know."

01:05:48.840 --> 01:05:50.880
I'm like, "Yeah let's go to 31 ice cream."

01:05:50.880 --> 01:05:53.455
And I went and it's a Baskin-Robbins.

01:05:53.455 --> 01:05:54.494
(talk over each other)

01:05:54.494 --> 01:05:56.370
It's just a fucking Baskin-Robbins.

01:05:56.370 --> 01:05:58.357
And I'm like, "You mean Baskin-Robbins?

01:05:58.357 --> 01:05:59.190
"Yeah, we have that.

01:05:59.190 --> 01:06:00.570
And she's like, "Baskin what?"

01:06:00.570 --> 01:06:02.644
And I'm like, "It says it right there."

01:06:02.644 --> 01:06:03.942
(laughter)

01:06:03.942 --> 01:06:05.222
"In English." (laughter)

01:06:05.222 --> 01:06:07.470
- We just highlight the 31 part.

01:06:07.470 --> 01:06:09.690
- If anything, it's harder to see the 31,

01:06:09.690 --> 01:06:12.280
than you see the Baskin-Robbins.

01:06:12.280 --> 01:06:13.680
- Because at the corner,

01:06:13.680 --> 01:06:16.070
it just says 31.

01:06:16.070 --> 01:06:19.640
- But I'm like, "Do you clearly
not see that on either side

01:06:19.640 --> 01:06:22.760
of the three and the one
it says Baskin-Robbins?"

01:06:22.760 --> 01:06:25.357
And she's like, "Oh my God,

01:06:25.357 --> 01:06:26.587
"I never saw that."

01:06:28.572 --> 01:06:32.570
It's like 31 is 5% of the logo.

01:06:32.570 --> 01:06:33.403
- That's crazy."

01:06:33.403 --> 01:06:34.990
- And you're just completely disregarding

01:06:34.990 --> 01:06:36.930
the other 95% of the logo.

01:06:38.390 --> 01:06:40.120
The Japanese love to do
that though, don't they?

01:06:40.120 --> 01:06:42.940
They love to take Western brands

01:06:42.940 --> 01:06:45.350
but completely change the name of it,

01:06:45.350 --> 01:06:47.340
just to fit their like way of things.

01:06:47.340 --> 01:06:49.280
I love how

01:06:49.280 --> 01:06:53.230
in Japan, they don't call
Mercedes-Benz, Mercedes-Benz.

01:06:53.230 --> 01:06:54.430
They just call it Bensu.

01:06:55.817 --> 01:06:57.397
- Bemz?

01:06:57.397 --> 01:07:01.197
- You know what they call
a Mercedes-Benz in Japan?

01:07:03.030 --> 01:07:05.050
- Because they can't pronounce Mercedes.

01:07:05.050 --> 01:07:07.068
'Cause when I said that,

01:07:07.068 --> 01:07:09.157
they were like, "What is Benz?

01:07:09.157 --> 01:07:10.637
"Benz is an acronym?

01:07:10.637 --> 01:07:11.850
"Benz is short for something?"

01:07:11.850 --> 01:07:13.957
And I'm like, "Yeah. It's Mercedes-Benz."

01:07:15.166 --> 01:07:16.720
Their minds were just blown.

01:07:16.720 --> 01:07:18.190
They were like, "Mercedes,
where did that come from?"

01:07:18.190 --> 01:07:20.810
- I wanna know the conversation
where Mercedes-Benz came up.

01:07:20.810 --> 01:07:23.400
That feels like a code word
for something I would never say

01:07:23.400 --> 01:07:25.568
like if I need help, Mercedes-Benz.

01:07:25.568 --> 01:07:26.401
(laughter)

01:07:26.401 --> 01:07:28.070
- No, because it was in
the same conversation

01:07:28.070 --> 01:07:30.010
of when I told my cousin that 31

01:07:30.010 --> 01:07:31.478
is called Baskin-Robbins.

01:07:31.478 --> 01:07:33.210
- You were just speed running the-

01:07:33.210 --> 01:07:35.167
- So I had to make sure I was like,

01:07:35.167 --> 01:07:37.310
"What do you call Mercedes-Benz?"

01:07:37.310 --> 01:07:38.978
'Cause I guess I just saw a Mercedes-Benz.

01:07:38.978 --> 01:07:41.245
- What do you call a
quarter of pound of cheese.

01:07:41.245 --> 01:07:43.820
- Quarter pound with cheese.

01:07:43.820 --> 01:07:47.427
- Maybe we try to keep the
same name, like Ben &amp; Jerry's.

01:07:47.427 --> 01:07:49.310
Kinda like you guys try to keep,

01:07:49.310 --> 01:07:52.240
not you guys, but anime in general,

01:07:52.240 --> 01:07:53.073
we just call it cheese.

01:07:53.073 --> 01:07:56.190
But now we have the same title.

01:07:56.190 --> 01:07:59.524
We have the same OPs and ending songs.

01:07:59.524 --> 01:08:01.090
- What do you think about the other way?

01:08:01.090 --> 01:08:05.030
How some anime series
completely change the name

01:08:05.030 --> 01:08:07.323
of the anime to fit the American way?

01:08:08.850 --> 01:08:10.620
What do you think about
how Detective Conan

01:08:10.620 --> 01:08:12.350
is called Case Closed?

01:08:12.350 --> 01:08:14.160
- I understand the name Conan

01:08:15.232 --> 01:08:16.782
it means-

01:08:16.782 --> 01:08:17.615
- It is, isn't it?

01:08:17.615 --> 01:08:18.448
Why?

01:08:18.448 --> 01:08:20.620
- Why not just Detective Conan?

01:08:20.620 --> 01:08:24.380
- It's because of the host
that's too famous in the State.

01:08:24.380 --> 01:08:26.080
- The hostage?

01:08:26.080 --> 01:08:27.737
- Conan.

01:08:27.737 --> 01:08:29.318
The talk show host.

01:08:29.318 --> 01:08:30.677
- Yeah, the talk show host.
- Detective Conan.

01:08:30.677 --> 01:08:34.460
- And also the characters name
that Schwarzenegger played

01:08:34.460 --> 01:08:36.129
back in the '90s. (talk over each other)

01:08:36.129 --> 01:08:37.962
- Conan the Barbarian.

01:08:39.410 --> 01:08:41.540
- People had Conan as him in English.

01:08:41.540 --> 01:08:42.470
- That's fair enough.

01:08:42.470 --> 01:08:44.110
At the time, I think,
it was coming around,

01:08:44.110 --> 01:08:45.050
they were really big.

01:08:45.050 --> 01:08:46.415
- Detective Conan O'Brien.

01:08:46.415 --> 01:08:47.540
(laughter)

01:08:47.540 --> 01:08:48.750
I wanna see that now.

01:08:48.750 --> 01:08:51.330
- I wanna see that show
when he becomes detective.

01:08:51.330 --> 01:08:53.030
- I think we have to change the name

01:08:53.030 --> 01:08:55.400
of a certain child back.

01:08:55.400 --> 01:08:56.763
Was it from Germany?

01:08:59.660 --> 01:09:02.223
In Japan, we called him Tantan.

01:09:03.503 --> 01:09:07.080
Tantan is a boy who got a dog with him.

01:09:07.080 --> 01:09:07.913
- It's Tintin?

01:09:07.913 --> 01:09:08.746
- Yes.

01:09:08.746 --> 01:09:12.447
But Tintin sounds like a
male genitalia in Japanese.

01:09:14.663 --> 01:09:16.268
(laughter)

01:09:16.268 --> 01:09:17.435
- I know that.

01:09:19.990 --> 01:09:21.977
- That makes sense though.

01:09:21.977 --> 01:09:23.890
- So we got our own reasons.

01:09:23.890 --> 01:09:26.120
- That's why me and my Japanese friends

01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:29.090
used to refer to the
male genitalia as a joke

01:09:29.090 --> 01:09:30.270
because we didn't wanna say

01:09:30.270 --> 01:09:31.400
the actual thing in public.

01:09:31.400 --> 01:09:34.019
So when we were in public we
would just be like Tintin.

01:09:34.019 --> 01:09:35.008
I'm curious.

01:09:35.008 --> 01:09:36.740
'Cause you've obviously been anime

01:09:36.740 --> 01:09:38.000
and manga fan your whole life,

01:09:38.000 --> 01:09:41.170
wat do you think about,
especially recently in the West,

01:09:41.170 --> 01:09:42.773
it's gotten really popular.

01:09:44.041 --> 01:09:46.117
Everyone's like, "I love anime."

01:09:47.060 --> 01:09:48.280
What do you think of, I guess,

01:09:48.280 --> 01:09:50.560
it getting bigger and all that?

01:09:50.560 --> 01:09:51.750
- I'm happy.

01:09:51.750 --> 01:09:56.070
At first, I thought some anime
titles that Western people

01:09:56.070 --> 01:10:00.040
know must be only Naruto and
Dragon Ball and that's it.

01:10:00.040 --> 01:10:01.750
But it's not true.

01:10:01.750 --> 01:10:04.650
They actually know and
they actually get to watch

01:10:04.650 --> 01:10:08.190
the same title at the same
time with English sub.

01:10:08.190 --> 01:10:10.308
- To be fair, a large
majority of anime fans

01:10:10.308 --> 01:10:13.760
still only watch Naruto and Dragon Ball.

01:10:13.760 --> 01:10:15.550
- That's a huge group.

01:10:15.550 --> 01:10:17.250
- Some people never get out of that phase

01:10:17.250 --> 01:10:19.330
and then some people
they now they just watch

01:10:19.330 --> 01:10:23.290
everything, like me, I guess.

01:10:23.290 --> 01:10:27.460
- As you said, before I
think the general idea

01:10:27.460 --> 01:10:29.677
of a Western anime fan
was like, "I love Naruto.

01:10:29.677 --> 01:10:30.510
"I love Dragon Ball.

01:10:30.510 --> 01:10:31.343
"I love One Piece."

01:10:31.343 --> 01:10:32.600
And then that was it.

01:10:32.600 --> 01:10:34.470
- What was the first US con you went to

01:10:34.470 --> 01:10:35.870
or your first experience of-

01:10:35.870 --> 01:10:38.233
- It was actually AX so the biggest one.

01:10:39.530 --> 01:10:40.370
- That's a common go-to.

01:10:40.370 --> 01:10:43.120
- I don't even think AX really counts.

01:10:43.120 --> 01:10:44.340
It's not really representative

01:10:44.340 --> 01:10:46.190
of a lot of other US conventions.

01:10:46.190 --> 01:10:47.023
Because

01:10:47.023 --> 01:10:50.600
AX is so big that it's a whole different

01:10:50.600 --> 01:10:51.518
experience from most other conventions.

01:10:51.518 --> 01:10:53.440
- You've got a lot of
Japanese industry people,

01:10:53.440 --> 01:10:55.850
so you hear a lot of Japanese at AX.

01:10:55.850 --> 01:10:57.450
Yeah, definitely.

01:10:57.450 --> 01:10:59.247
- Have you ever been to the smaller cons?

01:10:59.247 --> 01:11:00.080
- Yes, I have.

01:11:00.080 --> 01:11:01.316
So that was completely different.

01:11:01.316 --> 01:11:04.578
Some cons are just fan-based,

01:11:04.578 --> 01:11:06.270
no industry people there.

01:11:06.270 --> 01:11:07.930
- Very unorganized.

01:11:07.930 --> 01:11:10.410
Every single time I've
been a guest at a con

01:11:10.410 --> 01:11:12.850
something has gone horribly wrong

01:11:12.850 --> 01:11:14.633
with my flight, my hotel.

01:11:16.348 --> 01:11:17.430
- I think I've been pretty lucky.

01:11:17.430 --> 01:11:20.560
I've had a few cons where it was horrible.

01:11:20.560 --> 01:11:23.260
But a lot of the times,
especially the small cons,

01:11:23.260 --> 01:11:25.890
I have more fun at a smaller
con than say the others.

01:11:25.890 --> 01:11:27.360
- If I get there.

01:11:27.360 --> 01:11:30.740
One time, this con booked me

01:11:30.740 --> 01:11:31.820
months in advance.

01:11:31.820 --> 01:11:33.750
And I don't think they'd ever
had an international guest.

01:11:33.750 --> 01:11:34.583
So I told them like,

01:11:34.583 --> 01:11:35.970
"Hey, you should book flight soon

01:11:35.970 --> 01:11:37.617
'cause you're in the middle
of nowhere in the US."

01:11:37.617 --> 01:11:39.690
It was in Indiana.

01:11:39.690 --> 01:11:40.947
I was like, "You need to book flights.

01:11:40.947 --> 01:11:43.050
"'cause they don't happen
a lot from the UK."

01:11:43.050 --> 01:11:46.032
They didn't until one week before.

01:11:46.032 --> 01:11:48.914
And then I had to go on
a 35 hour flight path.

01:11:48.914 --> 01:11:50.833
- 35?

01:11:50.833 --> 01:11:52.530
- It should have been

01:11:52.530 --> 01:11:53.610
14 at most.

01:11:53.610 --> 01:11:55.760
- That was the cheapest
flight they could find.

01:11:55.760 --> 01:11:56.983
- That was the cheapest one.

01:11:56.983 --> 01:11:58.917
I asked them, I was like, "How much was

01:11:58.917 --> 01:12:02.376
"the other one that was,
I think it was 12 hours?"

01:12:02.376 --> 01:12:03.640
It's still long

01:12:03.640 --> 01:12:04.510
flight path.

01:12:04.510 --> 01:12:06.950
And they were like, "It
was 150 bucks more."

01:12:06.950 --> 01:12:09.252
And I'm like, "Are you kidding me?"

01:12:09.252 --> 01:12:10.523
- Why did you agree to this?

01:12:10.523 --> 01:12:12.410
- I already signed the
contract before that

01:12:12.410 --> 01:12:13.910
'cause they said they were
gonna buy the flights.

01:12:13.910 --> 01:12:16.111
And I thought they wouldn't do that to me.

01:12:16.111 --> 01:12:17.610
(talk over each other)

01:12:17.610 --> 01:12:20.250
That's a real rare moment there.

01:12:20.250 --> 01:12:22.500
- They wouldn't expect me
to turn up on my flight

01:12:22.500 --> 01:12:23.900
and then immediately do a panel

01:12:23.900 --> 01:12:25.720
within 30 minutes of arriving.

01:12:25.720 --> 01:12:28.080
And they did, they expected me to do that.

01:12:28.080 --> 01:12:29.660
- I've done that before.

01:12:29.660 --> 01:12:31.830
- And the worst part is
they booked me a hotel

01:12:31.830 --> 01:12:33.220
the night before that I missed

01:12:33.220 --> 01:12:34.730
because the 35 hour flight path.

01:12:34.730 --> 01:12:39.340
I'm pretty sure that hotel
room cost more than $150.

01:12:39.340 --> 01:12:41.470
So fuck you, that con.

01:12:41.470 --> 01:12:44.500
(laughter)

01:12:44.500 --> 01:12:47.730
- Every con's in Indiana
now is just sweating.

01:12:50.417 --> 01:12:52.350
- I've been to a bunch in Indiana

01:12:52.350 --> 01:12:55.917
and I've had a lot of the worst
experiences on that one con.

01:12:55.917 --> 01:12:57.280
- Why is it Indiana of all states?

01:12:57.280 --> 01:12:58.113
- I don't know why

01:12:58.113 --> 01:13:00.660
I've been to a lot of cons
in Indiana, for some reason.

01:13:00.660 --> 01:13:03.530
I went to one in Indiana,
which was Indy PopCon.

01:13:03.530 --> 01:13:05.320
That one was actually quite fun.

01:13:05.320 --> 01:13:07.750
I had a lot of fun with that one.

01:13:07.750 --> 01:13:10.160
Well first, it wasn't
really an anime convention.

01:13:10.160 --> 01:13:11.800
It was more like a YouTuber convention.

01:13:11.800 --> 01:13:14.920
So I think they were a
lot more used to getting

01:13:14.920 --> 01:13:16.370
all sorts of overseas guests.

01:13:17.277 --> 01:13:19.997
- Was your agent doing all
of that for you, the cons

01:13:19.997 --> 01:13:22.313
or was it you negotiating with them?

01:13:23.430 --> 01:13:25.450
- At AX, I was just an industry guest.

01:13:25.450 --> 01:13:27.533
So I was at a booth with other people.

01:13:27.533 --> 01:13:29.930
But at the smaller con I was a guest.

01:13:29.930 --> 01:13:34.242
So I got somebody from the
con with me all the time.

01:13:34.242 --> 01:13:36.001
- You had a handler.

01:13:36.001 --> 01:13:37.170
- I feel like 'cause I spoke English

01:13:37.170 --> 01:13:39.100
they all left me to my own devices.

01:13:39.100 --> 01:13:41.387
They were like, "Fuck it, just turn up.

01:13:41.387 --> 01:13:43.023
"We just expect you to be here."

01:13:43.023 --> 01:13:45.910
- I remember my first
time being a proper guest

01:13:45.910 --> 01:13:48.130
at a convention, I think
it was Crunchyroll expo

01:13:48.130 --> 01:13:49.930
because I had been guest before.

01:13:49.930 --> 01:13:51.960
But I remember that my first experience

01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:53.500
at Crunchyroll expo,
they gave me a handler.

01:13:53.500 --> 01:13:54.900
I'd had no experience.

01:13:54.900 --> 01:13:55.959
- What I do with you?

01:13:55.959 --> 01:13:57.150
(laughter)

01:13:57.150 --> 01:13:58.660
- He would just follow me around.

01:13:58.660 --> 01:14:00.840
And I would just feel so awkward.

01:14:00.840 --> 01:14:01.980
I would just be like-

01:14:02.830 --> 01:14:04.388
- Can you not?

01:14:04.388 --> 01:14:06.417
- I literally had to ask him to like,

01:14:06.417 --> 01:14:07.627
"Can you just chill?"

01:14:08.830 --> 01:14:10.930
'Cause I've heard a lot of
horror stories, so I get it now.

01:14:10.930 --> 01:14:12.510
But back then it was my first experience.

01:14:12.510 --> 01:14:14.507
So I'm like, "Dude, can
you just leave me alone?

01:14:14.507 --> 01:14:16.657
"I'm all good. I don't need any help.

01:14:16.657 --> 01:14:17.690
"I'm just walking around the con floor."

01:14:17.690 --> 01:14:19.590
- I feel bad every time I
wanted to go to bathroom

01:14:19.590 --> 01:14:20.780
because they have to follow me.

01:14:20.780 --> 01:14:23.133
And I'm like, "I'm sorry
I have a smaller bladder.

01:14:24.610 --> 01:14:26.117
"Sorry, I wanna go again."

01:14:28.260 --> 01:14:29.730
- I'm just very used to being left

01:14:29.730 --> 01:14:31.088
to my own devices as well.

01:14:31.088 --> 01:14:32.609
- I think it's a very
British thing as well.

01:14:32.609 --> 01:14:34.200
You're like, "I don't
want someone helping me.

01:14:34.200 --> 01:14:35.400
"I can do it on my own."

01:14:37.150 --> 01:14:38.550
- I think it's because I've had

01:14:38.550 --> 01:14:41.160
my fair share of really good handlers

01:14:41.160 --> 01:14:43.333
and just really useless handlers.

01:14:45.610 --> 01:14:47.260
I know how to use my handler now.

01:14:48.759 --> 01:14:50.336
(laughter)

01:14:50.336 --> 01:14:53.127
- I know how to use you
and abuse you if I want.

01:14:53.127 --> 01:14:54.349
(talk over each other)

01:14:54.349 --> 01:14:56.033
- I know how to maximize my handler.

01:14:57.720 --> 01:14:58.929
You know what I mean?

01:14:58.929 --> 01:15:00.840
- I'm gonna min-max this shit.

01:15:00.840 --> 01:15:02.566
- Joey turns up and he just gives him

01:15:02.566 --> 01:15:04.716
a fucking 10 page survey.

01:15:04.716 --> 01:15:06.740
He's like, "Fill this
out, I need to know."

01:15:06.740 --> 01:15:08.040
- Where's my Dom Perignon,

01:15:08.970 --> 01:15:10.830
the moment I land, come on guys.

01:15:10.830 --> 01:15:11.663
- Can I speak to you?

01:15:11.663 --> 01:15:12.800
I'm like, "This is bullshit."

01:15:12.800 --> 01:15:14.460
Joey's had really good experiences.

01:15:14.460 --> 01:15:17.820
And I feel like at least
half of my conventions

01:15:17.820 --> 01:15:20.450
that weren't AX had something massive.

01:15:20.450 --> 01:15:22.260
- It's really weird.

01:15:22.260 --> 01:15:24.590
You hear a lot of horror stories about AX

01:15:24.590 --> 01:15:25.930
from a lot of different people.

01:15:25.930 --> 01:15:27.030
I don't think I've had

01:15:28.120 --> 01:15:29.703
a horrible experience at AX.

01:15:32.800 --> 01:15:35.370
But I think it's also because my schedule,

01:15:35.370 --> 01:15:39.060
I purposely fill up my schedule
with as shit much to do

01:15:39.060 --> 01:15:42.310
so that I don't leave
enough room for error.

01:15:42.310 --> 01:15:43.437
Because a lot of people are like,

01:15:43.437 --> 01:15:44.657
"I'm gonna space everything out.

01:15:44.657 --> 01:15:48.040
"And then give myself some
time in between each thing."

01:15:48.040 --> 01:15:50.470
But I'm like, "No, that's
where the horror happens."

01:15:50.470 --> 01:15:53.040
It's the in between part
where you're left on your own.

01:15:53.040 --> 01:15:54.697
You're like, "Well, I guess I'll go

01:15:54.697 --> 01:15:56.240
"to the convention hall now."

01:15:56.240 --> 01:15:59.358
And then horrible things
happen at the convention hall.

01:15:59.358 --> 01:16:02.890
- AX has always been the
super, super busy convention.

01:16:02.890 --> 01:16:03.950
Everyone's always busy.

01:16:03.950 --> 01:16:05.490
Everyone's always doing something.

01:16:05.490 --> 01:16:07.030
What is your schedule like in AX?

01:16:07.030 --> 01:16:08.633
- I was signing.

01:16:11.337 --> 01:16:14.857
In the first year, they gave
me a 30 minutes break each.

01:16:14.857 --> 01:16:16.627
30 minutes isn't enough.

01:16:16.627 --> 01:16:19.775
I wanna take off my wig
'cause everything's cosplay.

01:16:19.775 --> 01:16:23.210
So I wanna take off my wig and

01:16:23.210 --> 01:16:24.043
shut myself

01:16:25.020 --> 01:16:26.270
in a bathroom stall

01:16:26.270 --> 01:16:27.770
or be myself.

01:16:27.770 --> 01:16:29.291
I just wanna take a rest.

01:16:29.291 --> 01:16:30.124
But I couldn't take a rest.

01:16:30.124 --> 01:16:32.407
I didn't want anyone to
see me without a wig.

01:16:33.250 --> 01:16:34.500
That would look horrible.

01:16:35.390 --> 01:16:36.790
- Unthinkable.

01:16:36.790 --> 01:16:39.630
Taking off a wig? No.
- Disgusting.

01:16:39.630 --> 01:16:42.540
- I just kept myself confided
in the stall, one stall.

01:16:43.830 --> 01:16:45.923
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

01:16:45.923 --> 01:16:48.513
And I took Asprin every single time.

01:16:49.734 --> 01:16:51.800
- I guess if you have
like a wig cap, that's

01:16:51.800 --> 01:16:53.323
stretching your head.

01:16:54.210 --> 01:16:56.360
- At some point I wanted stronger meds.

01:16:56.360 --> 01:16:58.880
So I had to like, "Could
you buy something?"

01:16:58.880 --> 01:17:00.400
- Give me meds.

01:17:00.400 --> 01:17:03.174
- In the States, I'm sure
they got stronger ones.

01:17:03.174 --> 01:17:04.940
Give me that.

01:17:04.940 --> 01:17:07.120
- I've never cosplayed before.

01:17:07.120 --> 01:17:09.800
And part of the reason is it feels like

01:17:09.800 --> 01:17:11.490
at a convention wearing a cosplay

01:17:11.490 --> 01:17:13.810
is a lot of effort and work

01:17:13.810 --> 01:17:15.643
to keep it intact.

01:17:16.620 --> 01:17:19.300
- I cosplayed once and that was at AX.

01:17:19.300 --> 01:17:22.330
And I cosplayed as Gintoki from Gintama.

01:17:22.330 --> 01:17:23.740
And I chose Gintoki

01:17:23.740 --> 01:17:26.350
not only because I like
Gintoki as a character

01:17:26.350 --> 01:17:29.740
but also because his stuff is light.

01:17:29.740 --> 01:17:30.573
It's a little more breathable.

01:17:30.573 --> 01:17:32.500
It's not like I'm wearing
a full suit of armor.

01:17:32.500 --> 01:17:34.557
So I'm like, "It's really hot.

01:17:34.557 --> 01:17:36.120
"This is a little bit breathable."

01:17:36.120 --> 01:17:37.240
I didn't take into account

01:17:37.240 --> 01:17:39.940
that I'd be wearing a
massive fucking white wig

01:17:40.812 --> 01:17:42.080
like Gintoki does.

01:17:42.080 --> 01:17:43.180
- That immediately is

01:17:43.180 --> 01:17:45.100
a heating thing on your head.

01:17:45.100 --> 01:17:48.820
- And because this part got so hot,

01:17:48.820 --> 01:17:50.480
it completely

01:17:50.480 --> 01:17:51.630
negated

01:17:51.630 --> 01:17:53.830
the free flowing clothes
that I was wearing.

01:17:54.688 --> 01:17:55.813
I remember I was in the
middle of a signing.

01:17:55.813 --> 01:17:57.340
I'm like, "I'm sorry, I can't."

01:17:57.340 --> 01:17:58.333
I just took it off.

01:17:59.468 --> 01:18:02.607
And I'm like, "I'm sorry.
Fuck the hair, I can't do it."

01:18:02.607 --> 01:18:03.440
I was like, "I don't care anymore.

01:18:03.440 --> 01:18:05.687
"I'm gonna take it off.
It's so hot in here."

01:18:07.000 --> 01:18:09.040
- I see some people in AX turning,

01:18:09.040 --> 01:18:11.690
rocking up in a full
Guts armor or something.

01:18:11.690 --> 01:18:13.497
I'm like, "How the fuck are you doing it?

01:18:13.497 --> 01:18:16.268
"It's 33 degrees Celsius here right now."

01:18:16.268 --> 01:18:18.150
- I guess if you just
restrict all your pores,

01:18:18.150 --> 01:18:19.320
you can't sweat.

01:18:19.320 --> 01:18:20.220
It can't come out.

01:18:20.220 --> 01:18:21.494
You can't come out.

01:18:21.494 --> 01:18:23.755
(talk over each other)

01:18:23.755 --> 01:18:24.588
- Very impressive.

01:18:24.588 --> 01:18:27.460
- That's why I wore a Virgin-Killer
sweater at AX one time.

01:18:28.610 --> 01:18:29.857
- That's breathable, right?

01:18:29.857 --> 01:18:31.967
(talk over each other)

01:18:31.967 --> 01:18:34.030
- Is that why you like cosplaying as girls

01:18:34.030 --> 01:18:35.860
because it's a breathable skirt?

01:18:35.860 --> 01:18:37.857
- I love skirts because

01:18:37.857 --> 01:18:39.800
you can free flow.
- You love skirts?

01:18:39.800 --> 01:18:42.020
I feel like I can stretch my full stretch.

01:18:42.020 --> 01:18:43.368
You know what I mean?

01:18:43.368 --> 01:18:45.400
- But you didn't get stopped by security.

01:18:45.400 --> 01:18:46.500
- No.
- Too much skin.

01:18:46.500 --> 01:18:48.717
- In LA, it's normal.

01:18:48.717 --> 01:18:52.183
I just went anything goes
in LA especially around AX.

01:18:53.060 --> 01:18:54.680
- I remember I got in the Uber

01:18:54.680 --> 01:18:55.767
and was seated with a guy.

01:18:55.767 --> 01:18:57.607
And the moment I sat in, he was like,

01:18:57.607 --> 01:18:59.116
"You're going to the
LA convention center?"

01:18:59.116 --> 01:19:00.594
(laughter)

01:19:00.594 --> 01:19:02.447
And I was like, "Yup, that's me."

01:19:03.310 --> 01:19:04.547
- They know now it's become a routine now.

01:19:04.547 --> 01:19:05.850
- And we didn't say anything.

01:19:05.850 --> 01:19:06.780
It was the most awkward thing.

01:19:06.780 --> 01:19:09.557
I was sitting there in the
back, like, "All right."

01:19:10.620 --> 01:19:12.495
Were you in a skirt at that time?

01:19:12.495 --> 01:19:13.364
- I was wearing the Virgin-Killer sweater.

01:19:13.364 --> 01:19:14.410
(laughter)

01:19:14.410 --> 01:19:16.460
I was cross-legged in the taxi like this,

01:19:17.644 --> 01:19:18.727
straddling my feet.

01:19:18.727 --> 01:19:21.902
(talk over each other)

01:19:21.902 --> 01:19:23.200
- I'm just crossing my legs.

01:19:23.200 --> 01:19:25.913
- You should have done the
Basic Instincts leg switch.

01:19:25.913 --> 01:19:26.746
(laughter)

01:19:26.746 --> 01:19:27.837
And then when he turns around like-

01:19:27.837 --> 01:19:29.387
- Like, "Ooh, hello."

01:19:30.580 --> 01:19:32.257
- I loved getting stopped by people.

01:19:32.257 --> 01:19:34.070
Like, "Can I take photos with you?"

01:19:34.070 --> 01:19:36.540
When you're a cosplayer that...

01:19:38.153 --> 01:19:40.810
I think the most popular cosplay at AX

01:19:40.810 --> 01:19:43.520
was Prison School that I wore.

01:19:43.520 --> 01:19:46.323
- That was, not the
president, the vice president.

01:19:48.629 --> 01:19:49.840
- I think that was last year.

01:19:49.840 --> 01:19:52.630
And one of the reasons I bet

01:19:52.630 --> 01:19:54.670
because it wasn't the
year for Prison School.

01:19:54.670 --> 01:19:58.830
So there weren't a lot of
Prison School cosplays.

01:19:58.830 --> 01:20:02.333
Most of them were wearing
Tamamo or Fate characters.

01:20:03.400 --> 01:20:05.109
- As it always is.

01:20:05.109 --> 01:20:06.720
- So I guess I stood out.

01:20:06.720 --> 01:20:08.177
And some father asked me,

01:20:08.177 --> 01:20:09.541
"Could you take a photo with my son?"

01:20:09.541 --> 01:20:11.920
And his son was tiny.

01:20:11.920 --> 01:20:15.100
- Did the son know what the series was?

01:20:15.100 --> 01:20:16.080
- Maybe it's the kid on the plane.

01:20:16.080 --> 01:20:19.200
- Oh my god, he probably was. (laughter)

01:20:19.200 --> 01:20:21.010
- Garnt watched Prison School on a plane

01:20:21.010 --> 01:20:24.360
and there was a tiny kid next to him

01:20:24.360 --> 01:20:26.050
It was that kid.

01:20:26.050 --> 01:20:28.101
He's like, "I love that show.

01:20:28.101 --> 01:20:29.141
"I saw it on a plane."

01:20:29.141 --> 01:20:30.942
(laughter)

01:20:30.942 --> 01:20:33.025
- Was that a plane to AX?

01:20:34.810 --> 01:20:36.050
- We talked about this before,

01:20:36.050 --> 01:20:37.550
I normally watch some shitty,

01:20:37.550 --> 01:20:40.370
I always have an anime photo

01:20:41.270 --> 01:20:42.103
on my tablet.

01:20:42.103 --> 01:20:42.936
Never watched that.

01:20:42.936 --> 01:20:45.875
Always watch shitty plane
movies most of the time.

01:20:45.875 --> 01:20:49.140
What's your favorite
cosplay that you'd say?

01:20:49.140 --> 01:20:51.540
Or is that like picking your children?

01:20:51.540 --> 01:20:53.190
- Can you name top five cosplays?

01:20:54.847 --> 01:20:56.950
- Actually, next week I'm doing

01:20:56.950 --> 01:20:59.750
my favorite character
from Final Fantasy VII.

01:20:59.750 --> 01:21:02.790
I've done Yuffie already
for obvious reasons.

01:21:02.790 --> 01:21:05.450
That's the most popular female character.

01:21:05.450 --> 01:21:08.573
And if you've got a chance
with that, go for it.

01:21:08.573 --> 01:21:09.803
But my favorite,

01:21:11.420 --> 01:21:12.900
is Yuffie.

01:21:12.900 --> 01:21:15.703
I just wanted to cosplay Yuffie.

01:21:15.703 --> 01:21:19.437
So I finally get to do that
next week, plus Cowboy Bebop.

01:21:21.023 --> 01:21:22.070
- Joe Valentine.

01:21:22.070 --> 01:21:24.220
- Not Joe Valentine, sorry
- Faye Valentine.

01:21:24.220 --> 01:21:26.250
- That's it, that's the
less than evil character.

01:21:26.250 --> 01:21:27.083
Faye Valentine.

01:21:28.010 --> 01:21:29.760
- What was your very first cosplay?

01:21:30.988 --> 01:21:31.821
- My own, right?

01:21:31.821 --> 01:21:32.860
- The Granblue Fantasy one?

01:21:32.860 --> 01:21:34.597
- That was fourth.

01:21:37.770 --> 01:21:40.343
Well, could be Super Sonico.

01:21:41.811 --> 01:21:42.644
I have no idea.

01:21:42.644 --> 01:21:44.540
(talk over each other)

01:21:44.540 --> 01:21:45.593
- I can see that happening.

01:21:45.593 --> 01:21:48.272
- That was also for me
as an industry guest.

01:21:48.272 --> 01:21:49.105
Actually,

01:21:50.008 --> 01:21:50.841
a boost too.

01:21:51.703 --> 01:21:53.541
So I don't know.

01:21:53.541 --> 01:21:55.180
my first,

01:21:55.180 --> 01:21:58.529
one of my own choice,

01:21:58.529 --> 01:21:59.679
I don't know.

01:21:59.679 --> 01:22:00.770
What was that?

01:22:00.770 --> 01:22:02.373
I did Mamako from-

01:22:03.768 --> 01:22:08.180
- From Her Two-Hit Attack.

01:22:08.180 --> 01:22:09.446
- Do you like your mother?

01:22:09.446 --> 01:22:10.279
(laughter)

01:22:10.279 --> 01:22:11.243
And Multi-attack.

01:22:13.116 --> 01:22:15.220
- That was such a terrible show.

01:22:15.220 --> 01:22:16.480
- We've talked about them before.

01:22:16.480 --> 01:22:19.000
- I think my favorite cosplay
that you've ever done was,

01:22:19.000 --> 01:22:20.150
I think it was at AX last year.

01:22:20.150 --> 01:22:21.570
You did Trish Una, right?

01:22:21.570 --> 01:22:22.403
- Yes, I did.

01:22:22.403 --> 01:22:24.933
- Your Trish cosplay
was really, really good.

01:22:24.933 --> 01:22:25.960
That was cool.

01:22:25.960 --> 01:22:27.500
- I'm obsessed with JoJo's.

01:22:27.500 --> 01:22:29.770
- We're all. We all love JoJo.

01:22:29.770 --> 01:22:33.231
Speaking of JoJo, you have
like the JoJo kimono, right?

01:22:33.231 --> 01:22:34.064
- Yes.

01:22:34.064 --> 01:22:34.972
That thing is so cool.

01:22:34.972 --> 01:22:36.630
- I ordered that in Osaka.

01:22:36.630 --> 01:22:37.463
- I would have ordered that.

01:22:37.463 --> 01:22:39.503
I don't care how much
it was, I'd have paid.

01:22:39.503 --> 01:22:40.680
Not even a question.

01:22:40.680 --> 01:22:42.283
- I'm gonna find out own Yahoo auction

01:22:42.283 --> 01:22:43.334
and (talk over each other)

01:22:43.334 --> 01:22:45.240
- That's where I get most
of my JoJo merch from.

01:22:45.240 --> 01:22:46.930
I'm using Google translate

01:22:46.930 --> 01:22:49.844
hoping I'm not clicking the
wrong things when I'm there.

01:22:49.844 --> 01:22:53.500
- Connor's become that stamp
collector but for JoJo's

01:22:53.500 --> 01:22:55.327
His grandkids are gonna be like.

01:22:55.327 --> 01:22:57.250
"What is all this?"

01:22:57.250 --> 01:22:58.840
- When I have a call with my parents,

01:22:58.840 --> 01:23:01.507
all my merchs are behind me,
like, "What are those toys?"

01:23:01.507 --> 01:23:02.570
"Connor, what are those toys?"

01:23:02.570 --> 01:23:03.403
Like, "It's not a toy, mum.

01:23:03.403 --> 01:23:07.107
"This is a one sixth gyro Zeppeli $200.

