Why are you familiar with them all?

02:03:53.372 --> 02:03:56.790
- I got a friend who loves
them, male and female.

02:03:56.790 --> 02:04:00.200
- I went to @Home in Akihabara.

02:04:00.200 --> 02:04:01.190
- Quintessential.

02:04:01.190 --> 02:04:03.847
- Because my friend who's a
huge fan of maid cafes was like,

02:04:03.847 --> 02:04:05.387
"You've never been to a a maid cafe?"

02:04:05.387 --> 02:04:06.327
"We should go.

02:04:06.327 --> 02:04:08.030
"I know the best one, it's @Home."

02:04:08.030 --> 02:04:09.604
I'm like, "All right."

02:04:09.604 --> 02:04:12.190
And man, I've never been more disappointed

02:04:12.190 --> 02:04:14.168
in a 2,000 Yen omurice in my life.

02:04:14.168 --> 02:04:15.340
(laughter)

02:04:15.340 --> 02:04:17.577
I'm like, "This thing costs 2,000 Yen?

02:04:17.577 --> 02:04:22.156
"And it took 45 minutes to
come out and it's cold."

02:04:22.156 --> 02:04:23.897
- And they put the spell on it.

02:04:23.897 --> 02:04:24.817
- And they put a spell on it.

02:04:24.817 --> 02:04:26.085
(talk over each other)

02:04:26.085 --> 02:04:28.067
- They do the moe moe kyun spell.

02:04:28.067 --> 02:04:30.320
And they force you to say it as well.

02:04:30.320 --> 02:04:31.837
- And I'm like, "I don't need a spell.

02:04:31.837 --> 02:04:32.959
"I need a microwave to heat this up."

02:04:32.959 --> 02:04:35.693
(laughter)

02:04:35.693 --> 02:04:38.757
"The spell isn't doing
anything but making it colder."

02:04:39.629 --> 02:04:40.462
- I think the most awkward experience

02:04:40.462 --> 02:04:42.480
in my life was having to do that.

02:04:42.480 --> 02:04:43.736
I was dressed as a maid

02:04:43.736 --> 02:04:46.262
and I had to do it at the airport.

02:04:46.262 --> 02:04:50.643
And there was 10 businessmen
who were watching.

02:04:52.533 --> 02:04:54.750
They were all not saying anything,

02:04:54.750 --> 02:04:56.671
not laughing, whenever I did anything.

02:04:56.671 --> 02:04:57.504
They would just stare.

02:04:57.504 --> 02:04:58.337
It was horrible

02:04:58.337 --> 02:05:01.125
because these girls are
really awkward as maids.

02:05:01.125 --> 02:05:02.323
I thought they were
supposed to be like, "Wow."

02:05:02.323 --> 02:05:04.073
But they were like...

02:05:07.400 --> 02:05:09.440
And then I had to draw on the omurice.

02:05:09.440 --> 02:05:12.053
I drew Sonik. (laughter)

02:05:13.170 --> 02:05:14.003
With ketchup?

02:05:14.003 --> 02:05:14.836
- Yeah, with ketchup.

02:05:14.836 --> 02:05:16.510
- And it was like diffusing a bomb.

02:05:16.510 --> 02:05:18.162
It was so tense in that room.

02:05:18.162 --> 02:05:21.070
Everyone was silent while I was doing.

02:05:21.070 --> 02:05:22.993
I'm sweating.

02:05:22.993 --> 02:05:23.826
- That's torture.

02:05:23.826 --> 02:05:26.210
- I'm like, "Can someone
break the silence,

02:05:26.210 --> 02:05:27.345
do something funny?"

02:05:27.345 --> 02:05:28.760
And whenever I made a joke, obviously,

02:05:28.760 --> 02:05:30.040
'cause none of them could speak English,

02:05:30.040 --> 02:05:31.000
they were like...

02:05:31.000 --> 02:05:33.030
- To break the silence,
you should have been

02:05:33.030 --> 02:05:35.194
under your breath be like,
(hums video game tune)

02:05:35.194 --> 02:05:37.444
(laughter)

02:05:40.160 --> 02:05:42.145
- So you like maid cafes?

02:05:42.145 --> 02:05:44.120
- My friend love maid cafes.

02:05:44.120 --> 02:05:45.420
I don't go there by myself.

02:05:45.420 --> 02:05:47.843
I'm not that avid religious.

02:05:49.280 --> 02:05:51.403
- Because there are some
religious people that go.

02:05:51.403 --> 02:05:52.680
- There's people that
go to every maid cafe

02:05:52.680 --> 02:05:54.720
and just rate every maid cafe.

02:05:54.720 --> 02:05:56.457
Like, "This maid was pretty cute.

02:05:56.457 --> 02:05:57.667
"She said moe moe kyun

02:05:59.792 --> 02:06:01.319
"the way I wanted to hear it."

02:06:01.319 --> 02:06:03.107
- It's different, that moe moe.

02:06:03.107 --> 02:06:05.130
- That moe moe came a bit different.

02:06:05.130 --> 02:06:06.450
- I saw a guy.

02:06:06.450 --> 02:06:07.950
He's a guy in Japan who has reviewed

02:06:07.950 --> 02:06:09.723
every Starbucks in Japan.

02:06:10.790 --> 02:06:12.570
Every single Starbucks in
Japan, I think he's reviewed.

02:06:12.570 --> 02:06:14.370
- Is he a Japanese?

02:06:14.370 --> 02:06:15.660
- Japanese guy

02:06:15.660 --> 02:06:17.930
I think there's plus 10,000.

02:06:17.930 --> 02:06:18.873
- Jesus Christ.

02:06:18.873 --> 02:06:20.020
I think that's all of the,

02:06:20.020 --> 02:06:20.853
- Nearly all of them.

02:06:20.853 --> 02:06:21.889
I think he's working his way through it.

02:06:21.889 --> 02:06:24.440
He's still going but he's
done over half, I know.

02:06:24.440 --> 02:06:26.890
- How different could they be?

02:06:26.890 --> 02:06:27.723
- That's what I think.

02:06:27.723 --> 02:06:30.649
I'm like, "You picked
the worst coffee chain."

02:06:30.649 --> 02:06:33.209
- Is that about the customer servicing?

02:06:33.209 --> 02:06:34.042
- I don't know.

02:06:34.042 --> 02:06:36.590
- I understand if he went around to go

02:06:36.590 --> 02:06:39.110
every independently-owned coffee shop

02:06:39.110 --> 02:06:41.180
because there's little differences

02:06:41.180 --> 02:06:43.730
but I'm pretty sure a
Starbucks in Hokkaido

02:06:43.730 --> 02:06:46.508
is gonna be the same
Starbucks as in Okinawa.

02:06:46.508 --> 02:06:49.153
- Maybe he cares about what the cup says

02:06:49.153 --> 02:06:50.253
with the doodle.

02:06:51.268 --> 02:06:53.960
- I'm gonna go to
Hokkaido to find that out.

02:06:53.960 --> 02:06:57.250
So I noticed that you're
a huge fan of retro games.

02:06:57.250 --> 02:06:58.083
- Yeah.

02:06:59.078 --> 02:07:01.410
(talk over each other)

02:07:01.410 --> 02:07:03.030
- Could you tell us some of
your favorite retro games?

02:07:03.030 --> 02:07:03.863
I'm interested.

02:07:04.965 --> 02:07:05.903
Or is that too hard?

02:07:05.903 --> 02:07:10.384
- The one I played most
was Cedar Moon action game.

02:07:10.384 --> 02:07:11.217
- Really?

02:07:11.217 --> 02:07:14.270
- It's very, very Final Fightish.

02:07:14.270 --> 02:07:15.540
- Is that the fighting game?

02:07:15.540 --> 02:07:17.600
- No, it's action game.

02:07:17.600 --> 02:07:18.940
It's exactly like final fight.

02:07:18.940 --> 02:07:20.978
You just keep walking and
some- (talk over each other)

02:07:20.978 --> 02:07:23.320
- Like Double Edged.

02:07:23.320 --> 02:07:26.603
- We call in Japan,
belt score action game.

02:07:27.780 --> 02:07:28.613
Keep going.

02:07:30.760 --> 02:07:34.070
- I think my cousin had a collection,

02:07:34.070 --> 02:07:35.310
'cause there was a number of them.

02:07:35.310 --> 02:07:37.543
There was six or seven
of them on the forum.

02:07:37.543 --> 02:07:40.720
- At least two family
game were action games

02:07:40.720 --> 02:07:43.880
and one puzzle game, one RPG,

02:07:43.880 --> 02:07:45.184
two fighting games.

02:07:45.184 --> 02:07:46.510
There are a lot of titles.

02:07:46.510 --> 02:07:48.073
- I saw you were streaming.

02:07:49.132 --> 02:07:50.877
Island Galleon game you were streaming.

02:07:51.990 --> 02:07:56.990
- I play the first PlayStation
ever game for PlayStation.

02:07:57.278 --> 02:07:58.800
It was simulation game.

02:07:58.800 --> 02:08:01.790
So you think you choose a certain

02:08:02.741 --> 02:08:03.574
answer.

02:08:03.574 --> 02:08:04.780
And that's gonna change the ending.

02:08:04.780 --> 02:08:06.683
But actually, until the very end,

02:08:08.000 --> 02:08:09.520
it's always the same.

02:08:09.520 --> 02:08:12.550
Up to the very end this final stream

02:08:12.550 --> 02:08:15.449
gonna let you choose three
paths and three endings.

02:08:15.449 --> 02:08:18.524
(talk over each other)

02:08:18.524 --> 02:08:21.010
- So it was basically
just mass effect then.

02:08:21.010 --> 02:08:22.910
Your choices mean nothing.

02:08:22.910 --> 02:08:23.743
- You know what?

02:08:23.743 --> 02:08:25.320
You can't even skip

02:08:25.320 --> 02:08:26.200
any stories.

02:08:26.200 --> 02:08:27.900
You have to rewatch it again and again.

02:08:27.900 --> 02:08:29.300
- That is the worst nightmare.

02:08:29.300 --> 02:08:30.600
- That's my hell.

02:08:30.600 --> 02:08:32.820
- I love the old Neo Geo games,

02:08:32.820 --> 02:08:34.640
Metal Slug is my favorite series.

02:08:34.640 --> 02:08:36.450
I fucking love Metal Slug.

02:08:36.450 --> 02:08:37.880
- I recently just did a video

02:08:37.880 --> 02:08:40.930
where I went and played
a bunch of Japan only

02:08:40.930 --> 02:08:42.863
retro games, anime retro games.

02:08:44.680 --> 02:08:47.210
Because there's a number
of JoJo games as well,

02:08:47.210 --> 02:08:49.894
like Superfamily con and-

02:08:49.894 --> 02:08:50.727
Hakirah

02:08:50.727 --> 02:08:51.730
- And the Yu Yu Hakusho game.

02:08:51.730 --> 02:08:54.017
- Dude, the Yu Yu Hakusho game was so fun.

02:08:54.017 --> 02:08:55.480
But I didn't realize that

02:08:55.480 --> 02:08:58.230
it's a really popular game in Japan.

02:08:58.230 --> 02:08:59.670
No one in the West knows about it

02:08:59.670 --> 02:09:02.200
because they only localized it.

02:09:02.200 --> 02:09:03.830
Well, obviously they only released

02:09:03.830 --> 02:09:06.043
in Japan and for some reason, Brazil.

02:09:07.127 --> 02:09:08.600
But only Brazil.

02:09:08.600 --> 02:09:11.090
The US didn't get it,
Europe didn't get it.

02:09:11.090 --> 02:09:11.990
Australia didn't get it.

02:09:11.990 --> 02:09:13.890
It was only Brazil that got it.

02:09:13.890 --> 02:09:17.980
- There are maybe a lot of
Japanese Brazilians at the time.

02:09:17.980 --> 02:09:19.680
- I found this out today actually.

02:09:20.582 --> 02:09:24.593
The legendary professional
wrestler, Antonio Inoki.

02:09:24.593 --> 02:09:27.030
He was from Brazil.

02:09:27.030 --> 02:09:27.925
- That's right.

02:09:27.925 --> 02:09:29.230
- Apparently there's a huge population

02:09:29.230 --> 02:09:30.210
of Japanese in Brazil.

02:09:30.210 --> 02:09:32.491
I can't remember the reason why .

02:09:32.491 --> 02:09:35.060
- Anime is pretty big
in Brazil so I've heard.

02:09:35.060 --> 02:09:36.780
Way bigger than it was,

02:09:36.780 --> 02:09:37.960
where we grew up.

02:09:37.960 --> 02:09:40.330
But it's just amazing how many anime games

02:09:40.330 --> 02:09:41.570
there are that have just existed

02:09:41.570 --> 02:09:44.730
that will never get translated.

02:09:44.730 --> 02:09:47.984
Even some big ones still
have not been translated.

02:09:47.984 --> 02:09:50.570
- 'Cause the Sierra Moon RPG one,

02:09:50.570 --> 02:09:52.830
they just got fans out a few years ago

02:09:53.790 --> 02:09:55.250
after all these years.

02:09:55.250 --> 02:09:57.200
- The original Fate/Stay
night visual novel

02:09:57.200 --> 02:09:59.310
has still not been officially translated.

02:09:59.310 --> 02:10:00.967
Really?
- Yeah.

02:10:00.967 --> 02:10:03.120
So anyone who's played the original

02:10:03.120 --> 02:10:04.150
Fate/Stay night visual novel,

02:10:04.150 --> 02:10:05.993
it's all fan translations right now.

02:10:06.950 --> 02:10:09.720
And Fate fans expect people
to get people into it

02:10:09.720 --> 02:10:11.020
by reading the visual novel.

02:10:11.020 --> 02:10:13.140
- Because I know it was
really massive news.

02:10:13.140 --> 02:10:16.560
I think it was like three
years ago when they decided

02:10:16.560 --> 02:10:17.439
to make an official
like English translation

02:10:17.439 --> 02:10:21.010
of the Clannad visual novel,

02:10:21.010 --> 02:10:23.380
and they'd made a kickstarter
for it and everything.

02:10:23.380 --> 02:10:26.430
And it got finished in less than 24 hours,

02:10:26.430 --> 02:10:27.760
even though it's such an old game.

02:10:27.760 --> 02:10:30.127
And it wasn't at that
point, I realized I'm like

02:10:30.127 --> 02:10:31.397
"Oh, shit, there's never been

02:10:31.397 --> 02:10:32.810
"an official translation of this game."

02:10:32.810 --> 02:10:34.220
It's all fan subs.

02:10:34.220 --> 02:10:37.890
And in my head, I'm like,
"Who is doing these fan subs?"

02:10:37.890 --> 02:10:42.095
Who has so much time
(talk over each other)

02:10:42.095 --> 02:10:43.260
and talent that you're
like, "You know what,

02:10:43.260 --> 02:10:45.327
"there's this visual novel,'

02:10:45.327 --> 02:10:46.917
"that's all dialogue,

02:10:46.917 --> 02:10:49.331
"200 plus hours long.

02:10:49.331 --> 02:10:52.797
"if you put into a script,
it's like 300, 400 pages.

02:10:52.797 --> 02:10:53.807
"I'ma translate it."

02:10:55.450 --> 02:10:57.270
How do you find yourself in that position?

02:10:57.270 --> 02:10:58.596
- Weebs weaponized, man.

02:10:58.596 --> 02:10:59.429
They're incredible.

02:10:59.429 --> 02:11:01.830
- Weebs are so passionate.

02:11:01.830 --> 02:11:02.920
- They are.

02:11:02.920 --> 02:11:04.160
Was it Secret of Mana

02:11:04.160 --> 02:11:06.120
that never got an official (indistinct)?

02:11:06.120 --> 02:11:07.850
- The first one, yeah.

02:11:07.850 --> 02:11:09.110
- Final Fantasy never got released,

02:11:09.110 --> 02:11:11.701
even though it was a huge
series until very recently.

02:11:11.701 --> 02:11:12.534
- Until very recently.

02:11:12.534 --> 02:11:14.780
- Which is crazy to think, a
game series like Final Fantasy

02:11:14.780 --> 02:11:17.200
that was killing it in the West as well.

02:11:17.200 --> 02:11:19.310
One of them wasn't released.

02:11:19.310 --> 02:11:20.143
That's crazy.

02:11:20.143 --> 02:11:20.976
- It's really weird.

02:11:20.976 --> 02:11:24.020
I have a lot of Mana's
fanatic friends in California,

02:11:24.020 --> 02:11:28.956
especially, but I think the
only official one was Robotech.

02:11:28.956 --> 02:11:31.960
Otherwise, you have to
look for them unofficially.

02:11:31.960 --> 02:11:34.290
- It's hard being a weeb. It's hard.

02:11:34.290 --> 02:11:36.933
- Especially a retro weeb
'cause now like Macross,

02:11:39.966 --> 02:11:43.160
it's not got as big of
a fan base as it used to

02:11:43.160 --> 02:11:46.320
because now Mecha has just almost died

02:11:46.320 --> 02:11:48.460
in the Western fandom.

02:11:48.460 --> 02:11:51.810
It's only the very dedicated
fans that still will keep

02:11:51.810 --> 02:11:52.820
up with everything like that.

02:11:52.820 --> 02:11:54.810
And if there is Mecha,
then it's usually combined

02:11:54.810 --> 02:11:57.573
with some other genre
that is more appealing.

02:11:58.420 --> 02:12:00.350
It's not usually Mecha is the main.

02:12:00.350 --> 02:12:02.007
It's like, "Here is the main

02:12:02.007 --> 02:12:03.953
"and we just add a little
bit of Mecha to it."

02:12:03.953 --> 02:12:05.300
- I think the last big Mecha

02:12:05.300 --> 02:12:06.457
was probably Dialing in the Franxx.

02:12:06.457 --> 02:12:08.580
and I'm pretty sure more people cared

02:12:08.580 --> 02:12:11.420
about Zero 2 than they cared about Mechs.

02:12:11.420 --> 02:12:13.237
No one was like, "Darling in the FranXX,

02:12:13.237 --> 02:12:14.579
"those mecchas are cool."

02:12:14.579 --> 02:12:15.937
It was more like, Darling in the FranXX,

02:12:15.937 --> 02:12:18.274
(talk over each other)

02:12:18.274 --> 02:12:19.126
- They were looking inside.

02:12:19.126 --> 02:12:20.770
- It's like, "Damn, that booty is thick."

02:12:20.770 --> 02:12:22.170
That's all they cared about.

02:12:23.810 --> 02:12:26.228
- We missed out on so many
good porn parodies, Japan

02:12:26.228 --> 02:12:28.040
because of your dumb laws
of Darling in the FranXX.

02:12:28.040 --> 02:12:29.620
Yeah. Oh my God.

02:12:29.620 --> 02:12:30.580
- I'm surprised they haven't made

02:12:30.580 --> 02:12:31.820
a Darling in the FranXX porn yet.

02:12:31.820 --> 02:12:33.900
Or in fact, so many anime series

02:12:33.900 --> 02:12:36.940
or manga series that could
easily make a porn parody.

02:12:36.940 --> 02:12:38.793
And I know it will sell.

02:12:40.232 --> 02:12:41.750
- Well, American porn producers who listen

02:12:41.750 --> 02:12:44.380
to Trash Taste, please make it happen.

02:12:44.380 --> 02:12:47.180
- Amen. We just gave you
guys free real estate.

02:12:47.180 --> 02:12:48.013
- Yeah, exactly.

02:12:48.013 --> 02:12:49.650
- 'Cause you know people
are gonna buy that shit

02:12:49.650 --> 02:12:51.050
if they make it in the West.

02:12:52.519 --> 02:12:55.069
- Macross, for example my
friend actually organized

02:12:56.864 --> 02:12:58.423
Macross convention, one day convention.

02:12:59.490 --> 02:13:01.320
It's called super dimension con.

02:13:01.320 --> 02:13:02.798
That's how much they love.

02:13:02.798 --> 02:13:04.000
- Is that in America?
- Yes.

02:13:04.000 --> 02:13:05.150
In California, I think.

02:13:06.350 --> 02:13:07.708
That's amazing that even though

02:13:07.708 --> 02:13:10.483
we didn't have an access
to the official ones.

02:13:11.740 --> 02:13:14.100
And also, I've noticed
that there are a lot

02:13:14.100 --> 02:13:17.485
of super fans in the West
because I played KonoSuba.

02:13:17.485 --> 02:13:18.817
- It's huge.

02:13:18.817 --> 02:13:21.800
- And every single time,
at least one person

02:13:21.800 --> 02:13:24.990
or I should say at least
10 people asking me

02:13:24.990 --> 02:13:27.363
every single time when
it's gonna be released,

02:13:28.670 --> 02:13:31.063
in the West, internationally.

02:13:33.649 --> 02:13:35.303
I know people like creators,

02:13:36.470 --> 02:13:39.440
they said they're only making available

02:13:39.440 --> 02:13:42.740
for Macao, Hong Kong,
Taiwan within this year,

02:13:42.740 --> 02:13:45.333
but not thinking about
English translation yet.

02:13:47.080 --> 02:13:48.270
- It's weird.

02:13:48.270 --> 02:13:51.490
They tend to really focus on
Southeast Asian countries.

02:13:51.490 --> 02:13:54.252
- It's because we spend the fucking cash.

02:13:54.252 --> 02:13:55.085
(laughter)

02:13:55.085 --> 02:13:56.413
What can I say?

02:13:57.710 --> 02:14:00.830
- 'Cause I remember, I guess
that at a con in Singapore

02:14:02.669 --> 02:14:04.290
and they were like sorts
of different booths

02:14:04.290 --> 02:14:06.550
with all these companies
were selling new stuff

02:14:06.550 --> 02:14:08.177
new merch and everything.

02:14:08.177 --> 02:14:12.700
And an American con, it's only
the diehard fans would go up

02:14:12.700 --> 02:14:15.167
and be like, "Give me one of everything."

02:14:15.167 --> 02:14:16.440
"Give me the most expensive thing.

02:14:16.440 --> 02:14:20.487
And it was just nuts to see so
many people just being like,

02:14:20.487 --> 02:14:22.750
"Give me this, give me
this, give me this."

02:14:22.750 --> 02:14:25.820
And people having five,
six bags worth of stuff.

